:::cell
header size
:::
:::cell
bounded by `ResourceLimits::signature_header_bytes` (default 8 KiB)
:::
:::
:::
::::

::::section {#trust}
## Trust separation

Cryptographic validity and trust are decoupled. `TrustPolicy::evaluate(header)`
returns the public key (or `untrusted_without_key()`); the verifier reports
`CryptographicStatus::Valid` independently of `TrustStatus::Trusted`.

:::note {type="info"}
A document with a tampered body but a still-trusted signer key returns
`CryptographicStatus::Invalid` + `TrustStatus::Trusted`. A valid signature
from an unknown key returns `Valid` + `Untrusted`. Hosts must combine both
fields before accepting a document.
:::
::::
